{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.corner_removal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.corner_removal","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L114-L147","doc":"**The corner-removal identity** (`lem:piece-a-corner-removal-obligation`).\n\nFor a removable corner `(r, s)` of `μ` (so `s + 1 = λ_r` and `λ_{r+1} ≤ s`),\n`1 + Σ_{j<s} (2 h(r,j) - 1) + Σ_{i<r} (2 h(i,s) - 1) = (s - r)² + 2 |μ| - 1`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:piece-a-corner-removal-obligation","label":"lem:piece-a-corner-removal-obligation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/piece-a-corner-removal-obligation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_cells_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_cells_split","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L91-L112","doc":"**Cell count by the corner's column.** `n = Σ_{j<s} colLen j + Σ_{i≤r} (λ_i - s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_row_tail_fiber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_row_tail_fiber","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L77-L89","doc":"The cells of `μ` in row `i` at columns `≥ s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_col_fiber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.card_col_fiber","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L64-L75","doc":"The cells of `μ` in column `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.row_le_of_col_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.row_le_of_col_ge","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L55-L62","doc":"A cell in a column `≥ s` lies in a row `≤ r`, because row `r + 1` and every\nrow below it have length `≤ s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.colLen_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.colLen_corner","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L46-L53","doc":"At a removable corner `(r, s)`, column `s` has exactly `r + 1` cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.two_mul_sum_range_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceACornerRemoval.two_mul_sum_range_id","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceACornerRemoval.lean#L37-L42","doc":"Twice the Gauss sum, over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}